# Build output. The artefacts the fixture needs are copied out of it by
# `regenerate.sh` (`module/nan_payloads.wasm.zst` and the instrumented
# pair under `page/`), so nothing here has to be committed.
wasm-src/target/

# The original module is committed as `module/nan_payloads.wasm.zst`; the
# expanded form is a local convenience the repo root's blanket `*.wasm`
# already ignores. `verify.sh` expands into a temp directory and never
# writes here.
#
# It is committed at all because it has to be *this* build: the offline
# replay runs the ORIGINAL, uninstrumented module (spec §6.1) and checks
# every recorded crossing against it, so a module compiled by a different
# toolchain — with different import indices or a different boundary
# signature — no longer matches the recording.
#
# It is committed *compressed* because the repo caps a committed file at
# 500 KB and the raw module is ~1.5 MB, almost entirely DWARF, which is
# the part the replay turns into per-line steps and locals and so cannot
# be stripped.
#
# `page/nan_payloads.instrumented.wasm` is deliberately not committed in
# any form. It is only needed to *re-record*, and `regenerate.sh` builds
# it together with a fresh recording, so those two cannot drift apart the
# way the original and the committed recording could.
